{
  "body_human_readable": "In 2024, Tesla's total deliveries amounted to approximately 1.79 million vehicles. More precisely, the company delivered 1,789,226 cars during the year.\n\nThis figure marks the first annual decline in deliveries for Tesla in 12 years, representing a slight decrease of about 1% from the 1,808,581 vehicles delivered in 2023.\n\nThe majority of these deliveries were composed of the Model 3 and Model Y, which together accounted for 1,704,093 units. The remaining 85,133 deliveries were of other models, including the Cybertruck. Despite the overall dip, the fourth quarter of 2024 set a new quarterly record for the company, with 495,570 vehicles delivered.",
